/T (Excluding children and ethical individuals from the workforce hinders national progress and poverty reduction. Their absence results in lost contributions to innovation, economic growth, and social improvement, perpetuating poverty and stifling creativity. Embracing diverse talents and ethical perspectives is essential for fostering an inclusive economy that can adapt to global challenges.)
